[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/en-US/docs/recipes/store-values.mdx:
  74: Provided by `@openmrs/esm-framework` (specifically, `esm-state`); this gives us access to [Zustand stores](https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand). This is useful for storing values that are shared across more than one component and need to be consistent across them. Note that while the underlying implementation uses Zustand, it is preferable to use the framework-provided APIs, such as [`createGlobalStore`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/createGlobalStore.md) and [`useStore`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/useStore.md), e.g.,
  77: import { createGlobalStore, useStore } from "@openmrs/esm-framework";
  89: const userStore = createGlobalStore<UserStore>("userStore", { user: null });
  102: Global stores are in memory by default. If a store needs to survive a browser refresh within the same tab session, pass `"sessionStorage"` as the third argument to `createGlobalStore()`.

[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs] content/fr-FR/docs/recipes/store-values.mdx:
  72: Fourni par `@openmrs/esm-framework` (spécifiquement, `esm-state`); cela nous donne accès aux [Zustand stores](https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand). Ceci est utile pour stocker des valeurs qui sont partagées entre plusieurs composants et qui doivent être cohérentes entre elles. Notez que bien que l'implémentation sous-jacente utilise Zustand, il est préférable d'utiliser les API fournies par le framework, comme [`createGlobalStore`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/createGlobalStore.md) et [`useStore`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/useStore.md), par exemple,
